PURPOSE

This repository publishes security-critical source code from the MyHRT
application (https://myhrt.health) so that anyone can read it, run it, and
independently verify the security claims MyHRT makes. It is published for
inspection and verification, not for reuse. This is source-available code, not
open-source software: the permissions granted below are limited to
verification, and all other rights are reserved.


PERMISSION

You are granted a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive permission to:

  1. View, read, and download the code in this repository.

  2. Build and run the code, including its test suite.

  3. Fork the repository on a code-hosting platform, and make local copies, for
     the purpose of inspecting, testing, or analyzing it.

  4. Quote or reproduce limited excerpts in security research, audits, reviews,
     reporting, or commentary, with attribution to MyHRT (Stuga Labs).

  5. Compare this code against a MyHRT application binary to confirm that they
     correspond.

These permissions exist so that you can satisfy yourself that the code does what
MyHRT says it does. No fee is charged for any of the above.


